@xuantengh I reproduced the reported failure on 8×B200. Across 3 repeated 8-rank runs, current main passed 24/24 and the PR tree passed 22/24. The two misses were both the existing non-GDN2 SBHD-vs-THD BF16 comparison: 6/131072 elements differed, with max abs error 0.00048828125 (one BF16 ULP; current tolerance 0.0003) and max relative error 0.03564453125. It was not deterministic, so I did not hide it by widening the tolerance.

The PR-specific normalization parity/end-to-end coverage and all deterministic GDN/GDN2 cases passed on every rank. Apex `fused_weight_gradient_mlp_cuda` imports successfully, and the HybridMoE constructor passed on all 8 ranks with 0 skips/failures. No traceback, NaN, or OOM was observed.

I also rewrote the four commit identities to my personal GitHub noreply address; the current head `f152abd9866da553a72d3b413fcdc7e69c7278f1` has a byte-identical source tree to the tested `3ce05c5f` head. DCO and the approval gate are green. Could you please re-review and `/ok to test f152abd9866da553a72d3b413fcdc7e69c7278f1`?
